    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23983" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">instĭtōrĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		institor, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>relating to</i>
			institores (post-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">operae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Ner. 21</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">artes, Hier. ap. Helv. 21: actio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					14, 3</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Gai. Inst. 4, 71</span></i>; <i><span class="en">74</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">instĭtōrĭa</span></b> ,
			ae, f., <i>a female
			broker</i> or <i>huckster</i>, <i><span class="en">Dig. 14, 3,
				5</span></i>.</div>
